> "Go and take out the trash, will you, honey?" is an imperative. If you
> tell me that it's also an order, I'll concede that we have different
> definitions of "order".


Okay, I concede that your example is of a request or suggestion, rather
than an order, despite its imperative.
But in general, imperatives and orders overlap a lot.
OTOH, I know that in Russian, sometimes--especially in the military--orders
are given in the infinitive.

